HOOKTEST: the DOS vectors through a program's own hooks, and ^C
  ok    INT 21h went through a hook and on to DOS
  ok    INT 2Fh went through a hook, and past it to the kernel's XMS
  ok    the INT 21h vector answers PUSHF/CALL FAR, as a TSR chains
  ok    INT 29h reached the screen
  ok    INT 25h read sector 0, both forms, flags left on the stack
  ok    INT 26h wrote it back and it reads the same
  ok    ^C, handler IRETs: the read is made again
  ok    ^C, handler RETF 2: the read is made again
  ok    ^C, handler RETF with carry clear: the read is made again
  ok    ^C, handler changes AH: that function is made instead
  ok    ^C, handler RETF with carry set: the child ends, 4Dh says ^C
  a child that ^C is about to end
  ok    ^C, no handler: the default ends the child, 4Dh says ^C
  ok    its own parent: 4Ch went to PSP:0Ah and the program carried on
  ok    INT 24h hooked by a child is put back when it ends
  ok    INT 2Fh AH=12h: install, 04h, 11h, 12h, 13h, 1Ah and 1Eh answer as DOS does
  ok    0Bh sees a key in the buffer, and 08h reads it
